> yes, say aloud this last phrase and hear the tone.

A tonal language is one in which changing the tone of a word turns it into =
a=20
different word. English has words in which changing which syllable is stres=
sed=20
turns them into different words (e.g. entrance), but no words in which chan=
ging=20
the tone turns them into different words.

Pierre
